riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2000: milkv-duos: switch USB to the type-A host port

The Milk-V Duo S has a single USB2 port shared between the type-A host
socket and the type-C device socket. Bringing DWC2 up in host mode is not
enough: two SoC GPIOs must be driven high to actually use the type-A
socket, mirroring the vendor's device/generic/rootfs_overlay/duos/
mnt/system/usb-host.sh:

  usb_select = XGPIOA[30] = porta 30 (pad AUX0)        -> FSUSB30 data mux
      (U9): 1 routes the SoC D+/D- to the type-A socket (else they stay on
      the type-C device socket).
  usb_en     = XGPIOB[5]  = portb 5  (pad USB_VBUS_EN) -> load switch
      (U10, SY6280AAC): 1 enables the type-A socket's 5 V VBUS.

Without the mux select, a device plugged into the type-A port never
enumerates even though the root hub is up and host mode is forced, because
the data lines are routed to the type-C connector -- the observed symptom
(no dmesg / lsusb change on hotplug).

An earlier version of this patch drove only VBUS, and on the wrong bit:
XGPIOB[6] / portb 6 is USB_VBUS_DET (USB_VBUS_DET__XGPIOB_6 = 3), an input
used for device-mode VBUS sensing, which the vendor *kernel* DTS happens
to reference as "vbus-gpio = <&portb 6>". The enable is XGPIOB[5]. The
XGPIO[n] == port[n] mapping is the same one already relied on for
CAM_RST0 (XGPIOA_2 == <&porta 2>) in patch 0024.

Mux both pads to GPIO (function 3) and hold them high with gpio-hogs; the
port is host-only so both stay asserted. AUX0 is on the 3.3 V VDDIO_EMMC
rail (same as the eMMC pins in patch 0023); USB_VBUS_EN is on 1.8 V
VDDIO18_1. Mux values are from the vendor pin list
freertos/cvitek/hal/cv181x/config/cv181x_pinlist_swconfig.h:
  USB_VBUS_EN__XGPIOB_5 = 3
  AUX0__XGPIOA_30       = 3

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
@@ -245,3 +245,62 @@
 &tempsen {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * USB type-A host mode (Duo S sheet 8, "USB HOST" + "USB SWITCH").
+ *
+ * The single USB2 port is shared between the type-A host socket and the
+ * type-C device socket. Two GPIOs put it in host mode, mirroring the
+ * vendor duos/mnt/system/usb-host.sh (which sets usb_select then usb_en):
+ *
+ *   porta 30 = XGPIOA[30], pad AUX0        -> FSUSB30 data mux (U9):
+ *       1 routes the SoC D+/D- to the type-A socket.
+ *   portb 5  = XGPIOB[5],  pad USB_VBUS_EN -> load switch (U10, SY6280AAC):
+ *       1 enables the type-A socket's 5 V VBUS.
+ *
+ * Without the mux select the data lines stay on the type-C socket and a
+ * device on the type-A port never enumerates despite host mode. NB
+ * XGPIOB[6]/portb 6 is USB_VBUS_DET (an input), not the VBUS enable.
+ *
+ * Both pads are muxed to GPIO (function 3) and held high by gpio-hogs --
+ * the port is host-only. AUX0 is on the 3.3 V VDDIO_EMMC rail (as the
+ * eMMC pins), USB_VBUS_EN on 1.8 V VDDIO18_1. Mux values from the vendor
+ * pin list cv181x_pinlist_swconfig.h: USB_VBUS_EN__XGPIOB_5 = 3,
+ * AUX0__XGPIOA_30 = 3.
+ */
+&{/soc/pinctrl@3001000} {
+	usb_host_pins: usb-host-pins {
+		usb-vbus-en-grp {
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_USB_VBUS_EN, 3)>;
+			power-source = <1800>;
+		};
+
+		usb-port-sel-grp {
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_AUX0, 3)>;
+			power-source = <3300>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&usb {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&usb_host_pins>;
+};
+
+&porta {
+	usb-port-sel-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <30 0>;		/* porta 30 = XGPIOA[30], USB_PORT_SEL */
+		output-high;		/* 1 = route D+/D- to type-A host socket */
+		line-name = "usb-port-sel";
+	};
+};
+
+&portb {
+	usb-vbus-en-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <5 0>;		/* portb 5 = XGPIOB[5], USB_VBUS_EN */
+		output-high;		/* 1 = enable type-A VBUS switch U10 */
+		line-name = "usb-vbus-en";
+	};
+};
